{"id": "ch40", "number": "40", "title": "Derived rules", "titleInlines": [{"type": "text", "text": "Derived rules"}], "part": "VII", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "As in the case of TFL, we first introduced some rules for FOL as basic (in "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:BasicFOL", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch36", "text": "chapter 36"}, {"type": "text", "text": "), and then added some further rules for conversion of quantifiers (in "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:CQ", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch38", "text": "chapter 38"}, {"type": "text", "text": "). In fact, the CQ rules should be regarded as "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "derived"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " rules, for they can be derived from the "}, {"type": "emph", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "basic"}]}, {"type": "text", "text": " rules of "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:BasicFOL", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch36", "text": "chapter 36"}, {"type": "text", "text": ". (The point here is as in "}, {"type": "ref", "label": "s:Derived", "variant": "cref", "href": "/read/ch21", "text": "chapter 21"}, {"type": "text", "text": ".) Here is a justification for the first CQ rule:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\forall x\\, \\lnot A(x)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "m+1", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\exists x\\, A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "m+2", "depth": 2, "hypo": true, "formula": "A(c)", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "m+3", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot A(c)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\forall", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m", "ruleText": "∀E"}, {"num": "m+4", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m+3, m+2", "ruleText": "¬E"}, {"num": "m+5", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\exists", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m+1, (m+2)–(m+4)", "ruleText": "∃E"}, {"num": "m+6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\exists x\\, A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "(m+1)–(m+5)", "ruleText": "¬I"}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Here is a justification of the third CQ rule:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "m", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\exists x\\, \\lnot A(x)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "m+1", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\forall x\\, A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "m+2", "depth": 2, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot A(c)", "rule": [{"type": "text", "text": "AS"}], "refs": "", "ruleText": "AS"}, {"num": "m+3", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "A(c)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\forall", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m+1", "ruleText": "∀E"}, {"num": "m+4", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m+2, m+3", "ruleText": "¬E"}, {"num": "m+5", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\exists", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "m, (m+2)–(m+4)", "ruleText": "∃E"}, {"num": "m+6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot \\forall x\\, A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "(m+1)–(m+5)", "ruleText": "¬I"}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "This explains why the CQ rules can be treated as derived. Similar justifications can be offered for the other two CQ rules."}]}], "exercises": [{"letter": "A", "blocks": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Offer proofs which justify the addition of the second and fourth CQ rules as derived rules."}]}], "items": [], "id": "ch40.A", "kind": "free", "sub": null, "logic": "fol", "hasKey": false, "solution": [{"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "Justification for the second rule:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot \\exists x\\,A(x)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "A(a)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\exists x\\,A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\exists", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "2", "ruleText": "∃I"}, {"num": "4", "depth": 1, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\bot", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "E"}], "refs": "3, 1", "ruleText": "¬E"}, {"num": "5", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\lnot A(a)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\lnot"}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "2–4", "ruleText": "¬I"}, {"num": "6", "depth": 0, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\forall x \\lnot A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\forall", "display": false}, {"type": "text", "text": "I"}], "refs": "5", "ruleText": "∀I"}]}, {"type": "para", "children": [{"type": "text", "text": "The fourth rule is harder to justify. Here is a proof that is relatively straightforward, but uses the derived rule DNE:"}]}, {"type": "fitch", "lines": [{"num": "1", "depth": 0, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot \\forall x\\,A(x)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "2", "depth": 1, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot \\exists x \\lnot A(x)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "3", "depth": 2, "hypo": true, "formula": "\\lnot A(a)", "rule": null, "refs": null}, {"num": "4", "depth": 2, "hypo": false, "formula": "\\exists x \\lnot A(x)", "rule": [{"type": "math", "latex": "\\exists", "display": false}, {"typ